<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="ASR" content="QuantumSPDF Masterclass">
  <meta name="keywords" content="Electronic Configuration, Aufbau Principle, SPDF Orbitals, Quantum Chemistry, Hund's Rule, Pauli Exclusion Principle">
  
  <style>
    /* Premium Typography & Variable Definitions */
    :root {
      --bg-dark: #0a0c10;
      --bg-card: rgba(20, 24, 35, 0.6);
      --border-glow: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.15);
      --cyan: #00f2fe;
      --blue: #4facfe;
      --purple: #d946ef;
      --purple-dark: #7f00ff;
      --text-main: #f3f4f6;
      --text-muted: #9ca3af;
      --success: #10b981;
      --danger: #ef4444;
      --transition-speed: 0.3s;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      background-color: var(--bg-dark);
      background-image: 
        radial-gradient(circle at 10% 20%, rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.05) 0%, transparent 40%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 90% 80%, rgba(217, 70, 239, 0.05) 0%, transparent 40%);
      color: var(--text-main);
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.6;
      overflow-x: hidden;
      padding-bottom: 60px;
    }

    /* Scroll Progress Bar */
    #scrollProgress {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      height: 4px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cyan), var(--purple));
      width: 0%;
      z-index: 1000;
      transition: width 0.1s ease-out;
    }

    /* Custom Scrollbar */
    ::-webkit-scrollbar {
      width: 10px;
    }
    ::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
      background: var(--bg-dark);
    }
    ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      border-radius: 10px;
      border: 2px solid var(--bg-dark);
    }
    ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
      background: var(--cyan);
    }

    /* Header & Navigation */
    header {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 100;
      background: rgba(10, 12, 16, 0.8);
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
      padding: 15px 5%;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .logo-container {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .logo-icon {
      font-size: 1.8rem;
      background: linear-gradient(45deg, var(--cyan), var(--purple));
      -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
      animation: pulse 2s infinite alternate;
    }

    .logo-text {
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cyan), var(--blue));
      -webkit-background-clip: text;
      background-clip: text;
      color: transparent;          /* ← replaced -webkit-text-fill-color */
    }

    .nav-actions {
      display: flex;
      gap: 15px;
    }

    /* Custom Premium Buttons */
    .btn {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
      color: var(--text-main);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      padding: 10px 20px;
      border-radius: 8px;
      font-weight: 600;
      cursor: pointer;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      transition: all var(--transition-speed) ease;
    }

    .btn:hover {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--cyan), var(--blue));
      color: #000;
      border-color: transparent;
      box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.4);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }

    .btn-purple {
      background: rgba(217, 70, 239, 0.1);
      border: 1px solid rgba(217, 70, 239, 0.2);
    }

    .btn-purple:hover {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--purple), var(--purple-dark));
      color: #fff;
      border-color: transparent;
      box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(217, 70, 239, 0.4);
    }

    /* Toast Notification */
    #toast {
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 30px;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(100px);
      background: rgba(20, 24, 35, 0.95);
      border: 1px solid var(--cyan);
      box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
      padding: 12px 24px;
      border-radius: 50px;
      z-index: 1000;
      opacity: 0;
      transition: transform 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.175, 0.885, 0.32, 1.275), opacity 0.3s;
      pointer-events: none;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
    }

    #toast.show {
      transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(0);
      opacity: 1;
    }

    /* Layout Containers */
    .container {
      max-width: 1200px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 20px;
    }

    /* Hero Section */
    .hero {
      text-align: center;
      padding: 80px 0 60px 0;
      position: relative;
    }

    .hero-badge {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 6px 16px;
      background: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.08);
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
      border-radius: 50px;
      color: var(--cyan);
      font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      animation: float 3s ease-in-out infinite;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 3.5rem;
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: -1px;
      line-height: 1.1;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff 30%, var(--cyan) 70%, var(--purple) 100%);
      -webkit-background-clip: text;
      background-clip: text;
      color: transparent;          /* ← replaced -webkit-text-fill-color */
    }

    .hero p {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto 35px auto;
    }

    /* Cards & Glassmorphism Grid */
    .glass-card {
      background: var(--bg-card);
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      border: 1px solid var(--border-glow);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 30px;
      margin-bottom: 30px;
      transition: border-color var(--transition-speed), box-shadow var(--transition-speed), transform var(--transition-speed);
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .glass-card::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 3px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cyan), transparent);
      opacity: 0.5;
    }

    .glass-card:hover {
      border-color: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.3);
      box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.05);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }

    /* Neon Section Titles */
    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      margin-bottom: 25px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
      color: #fff;
    }

    .section-title span {
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cyan), var(--purple));
      -webkit-background-clip: text;
      background-clip: text;
      color: transparent;          /* ← replaced -webkit-text-fill-color */
    }

    /* Grid Layouts */
    .grid-2 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
      gap: 25px;
    }

    .grid-3 {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: 25px;
    }

    /* Info Badge / Highlight Text */
    .highlight-card {
      background: rgba(217, 70, 239, 0.03);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--purple);
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
      margin: 20px 0;
    }

    .highlight-card h4 {
      color: var(--purple);
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
    }

    /* Orbitals Table */
    .premium-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 20px 0;
      text-align: left;
    }

    .premium-table th {
      background: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.05);
      border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
      padding: 12px 16px;
      color: var(--cyan);
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .premium-table td {
      padding: 12px 16px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
      color: var(--text-main);
    }

    .premium-table tr:hover {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
    }

    /* Orbital Box Fillings (Visualizer) */
    .orbital-visualizer {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 20px;
      margin-top: 15px;
    }

    .subshell-container {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .subshell-title {
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .orbital-boxes {
      display: flex;
      gap: 4px;
    }

    .orbital-box {
      width: 40px;
      height: 40px;
      border: 2px solid rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.3);
      border-radius: 6px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      background: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.03);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: var(--cyan);
      transition: all 0.3s;
    }

    .orbital-box.filled {
      border-color: var(--cyan);
      background: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.15);
      box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
    }

    .orbital-box.half-filled {
      border-color: var(--purple);
      background: rgba(217, 70, 239, 0.15);
      color: var(--purple);
      box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(217, 70, 239, 0.2);
    }

    /* Aufbau SVG Diagram Layout */
    .diagram-section {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
      gap: 40px;
      align-items: center;
    }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .diagram-section {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }

    .svg-wrapper {
      background: rgba(13, 16, 23, 0.8);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 20px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 20px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.05);
    }

    /* Solved Examples Grid & Expanders */
    .example-card {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 20px;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: all 0.3s;
    }

    .example-card:hover {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
      border-color: var(--cyan);
    }

    .example-header {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .example-element {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .element-symbol {
      display: inline-flex;
      width: 40px;
      height: 40px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--cyan), var(--blue));
      color: #000;
      font-weight: 800;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      border-radius: 50%;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .element-symbol.exceptional {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--purple), var(--purple-dark));
      color: #fff;
      box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(217, 70, 239, 0.3);
    }

    .example-body {
      max-height: 0;
      overflow: hidden;
      transition: max-height 0.4s ease-out;
      padding-top: 0;
    }

    .example-card.expanded .example-body {
      max-height: 500px;
      padding-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
      margin-top: 15px;
    }

    .toggle-icon {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      transition: transform 0.3s;
    }

    .example-card.expanded .toggle-icon {
      transform: rotate(180deg);
    }

    /* Interactive MCQ Quiz styling */
    .quiz-section {
      background: rgba(13, 16, 23, 0.7);
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2);
      box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.05);
    }

    .quiz-question-card {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 24px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .question-text {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
      color: #fff;
    }

    .options-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    @media (min-width: 768px) {
      .options-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      }
    }

    .option-label {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 14px 20px;
      cursor: pointer;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
      font-weight: 500;
      transition: all 0.2s;
    }

    .option-label:hover {
      background: rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.05);
      border-color: var(--cyan);
    }

    .option-label input[type="radio"] {
      appearance: none;
      -webkit-appearance: none;
      width: 18px;
      height: 18px;
      border: 2px solid var(--text-muted);
      border-radius: 50%;
      outline: none;
      transition: all 0.2s;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      position: relative;
    }

    .option-label input[type="radio"]:checked {
      border-color: var(--cyan);
      background: var(--cyan);
      box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--cyan);
    }

    .option-label input[type="radio"]:checked::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      width: 6px;
      height: 6px;
      background: #000;
      border-radius: 50%;
      top: 50%;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    }

    /* Scorecard Styling */
    .scorecard {
      display: none;
      background: rgba(20, 24, 35, 0.95);
      border: 2px solid var(--cyan);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 30px;
      margin: 30px 0;
      text-align: center;
      box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.15);
      animation: scaleIn 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.175, 0.885, 0.32, 1.275);
    }

    .score-circle {
      width: 140px;
      height: 140px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.2) 0%, transparent 80%);
      border: 4px dashed var(--cyan);
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      font-weight: 900;
      color: #fff;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .scorecard h3 {
      font-size: 1.8rem;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .scorecard p {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .stats-row {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 30px;
      margin-bottom: 25px;
    }

    .stat-box {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
      padding: 10px 20px;
      border-radius: 8px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    }

    .stat-num {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      font-weight: 800;
    }

    .stat-num.correct { color: var(--success); }
    .stat-num.wrong { color: var(--danger); }

    /* Evaluation styles */
    .option-label.correct-selected {
      background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.1) !important;
      border-color: var(--success) !important;
      color: var(--success) !important;
    }

    .option-label.incorrect-selected {
      background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.1) !important;
      border-color: var(--danger) !important;
      color: var(--danger) !important;
    }

    .option-label.correct-not-selected {
      border: 2px dashed var(--success) !important;
      color: var(--success) !important;
      background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.03);
    }

    /* Floating Back to Top Button */
    .back-to-top {
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 30px;
      right: 30px;
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: rgba(20, 24, 35, 0.8);
      border: 1px solid var(--cyan);
      color: var(--cyan);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      cursor: pointer;
      opacity: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
      transition: all 0.3s;
      z-index: 99;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.25);
    }

    .back-to-top.show {
      opacity: 1;
      pointer-events: auto;
    }

    .back-to-top:hover {
      background: var(--cyan);
      color: #000;
      transform: translateY(-5px);
    }

    /* Sequential reveal steps styling */
    .step-list {
      list-style: none;
    }

    .step-item {
      display: flex;
      gap: 15px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .step-number {
      width: 32px;
      height: 32px;
      background: var(--cyan);
      color: #000;
      font-weight: 800;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      border-radius: 50%;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .step-content h4 {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      color: #fff;
      margin-bottom: 5px;
    }

    .step-content p {
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }

    /* Animations */
    @keyframes pulse {
      0% { filter: drop-shadow(0 0 2px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.5)); }
      100% { filter: drop-shadow(0 0 12px rgba(0, 242, 254, 0.8)); }
    }

    @keyframes float {
      0% { transform: translateY(0); }
      50% { transform: translateY(-6px); }
      100% { transform: translateY(0); }
    }

    @keyframes scaleIn {
      from { transform: scale(0.9); opacity: 0; }
      to { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; }
    }

    .reveal-on-scroll {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(30px);
      transition: opacity 0.8s ease-out, transform 0.8s ease-out;
    }

    .reveal-on-scroll.visible {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }

    /* Print-Only Style Override */
    @media print {
      body {
        background: #fff !important;
        color: #000 !important;
      }
      header, .btn, .back-to-top, #scrollProgress, .quiz-section, .hero-badge, .nav-actions {
        display: none !important;
      }
      .glass-card {
        background: none !important;
        border: 1px solid #ddd !important;
        box-shadow: none !important;
        color: #000 !important;
        page-break-inside: avoid;
      }
      .section-title span, .logo-text, .hero h1 {
        color: #000 !important;
        background: none !important;
        -webkit-text-fill-color: initial !important;
      }
      .orbital-box {
        border-color: #000 !important;
        color: #000 !important;
      }
      .orbital-box.filled, .orbital-box.half-filled {
        background: none !important;
        box-shadow: none !important;
      }
    }
  </style>

<!-- Essential SEO Meta Tags -->
<% 
  const pageTitle = typeof title !== 'undefined' ? title : 'Quantum SPDF Configuration & Aufbau Rule Masterclass';
  const pageDesc = typeof description !== 'undefined' ? description : 'Master electronic configurations, spdf subshells, Aufbau rule, Hunds law, and Pauli principles with interactive visuals.';
%>
<title><%= pageTitle %></title>
<meta name="title" content="<%= pageTitle %>">
<meta name="description" content="<%= pageDesc %>">
<meta name="robots" content="index, follow">

<!-- Open Graph / WhatsApp Preview -->
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:title" content="<%= pageTitle %>">
<meta property="og:description" content="<%= pageDesc %>">
<% if (typeof url !== 'undefined') { %><meta property="og:url" content="<%= url %>"><% } %>
<% if (typeof image !== 'undefined') { %><meta property="og:image" content="<%= image %>"><% } %>

<!-- Twitter Card -->
<meta property="twitter:card" content="summary">
<meta property="twitter:title" content="<%= pageTitle %>">
<meta property="twitter:description" content="<%= pageDesc %>">
<% if (typeof url !== 'undefined') { %><meta property="twitter:url" content="<%= url %>"><% } %>
<% if (typeof image !== 'undefined') { %><meta property="twitter:image" content="<%= image %>"><% } %>

</head>
<body>

  <!-- Scroll Progress Indicator -->
  <div id="scrollProgress"></div>

  <!-- Header Navigation -->
  <header>
    <div class="logo-container">
      <span class="logo-icon">⚛️</span>
      <span class="logo-text">QuantumSPDF</span>
    </div>
    <div class="nav-actions">
      <button class="btn" onclick="copyConfigNotes()">
        <span>📋</span> Copy Notes
      </button>
      <button class="btn btn-purple" onclick="printPage()">
        <span>🖨️</span> Print Masterclass
      </button>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="container">
    
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="hero">
      <span class="hero-badge">Deep Dive Chemistry</span>
      <h1>Mastering Electronic Configuration</h1>
      <p>A comprehensive masterclass on how electrons arrange themselves inside atomic subshells ($s, p, d, f$) using the Aufbau rule, Hund's law, and Pauli's principles.</p>
      <a href="#quiz" class="btn">🚀 Challenge Yourself: 10-Question MCQ Quiz</a>
    </section>
    <div style="text-align: center; margin: 25px 0;">
      <a href="/bohr" target="_blank">How to change spdf configuration into Bohr Bury electronic configuration</a>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Intro -->
    <section class="glass-card reveal-on-scroll">
      <h2 class="section-title"><span>01.</span> Introduction to Electronic Configuration</h2>
      <p>
        In quantum chemistry, <strong>Electronic Configuration</strong> is the distribution of electrons of an atom or molecule in atomic or molecular orbitals. Rather than orbiting the nucleus in neat, planetary pathways, electrons exist in high-probability regional clouds called <strong>orbitals</strong>.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">
        Understanding how these configurations form is crucial because the electron arrangement in the outermost shell (valence electrons) directly determines an element's reactivity, bonding properties, and position in the periodic table.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section: SPDF Orbitals -->
    <section class="glass-card reveal-on-scroll">
      <h2 class="section-title"><span>02.</span> SPDF Subshells & Orbitals</h2>
      <p>
        The main energy levels (shells, defined by quantum number $n$) are split into subshells ($l = 0, 1, 2, 3$). These subshells are named <strong>s</strong> (sharp), <strong>p</strong> (principal), <strong>d</strong> (diffuse), and <strong>f</strong> (fundamental). Each subshell holds a maximum capacity of electrons determined by the number of individual spatial orbitals it possesses.
      </p>

      <table class="premium-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Subshell</th>
            <th>Azimuthal Quantum Number ($l$)</th>
            <th>No. of Orbitals ($2l + 1$)</th>
            <th>Maximum Electrons ($2(2l + 1)$)</th>
            <th>Orbital Shape</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>s</strong></td>
            <td>0</td>
            <td>1</td>
            <td><strong>2</strong></td>
            <td>Spherical</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>p</strong></td>
            <td>1</td>
            <td>3</td>
            <td><strong>6</strong></td>
            <td>Dumbbell-shaped</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>d</strong></td>
            <td>2</td>
            <td>5</td>
            <td><strong>10</strong></td>
            <td>Double Dumbbell</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>f</strong></td>
            <td>3</td>
            <td>7</td>
            <td><strong>14</strong></td>
            <td>Highly Complex</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="highlight-card">
        <h4>💡 Key Rule: The $2n^2$ Capacity</h4>
        <p>The maximum number of electrons that can occupy any principal energy shell $n$ is calculated using the formula <strong>$2n^2$</strong>. For example, for $n = 3$, the capacity is $2(3)^2 = 18$ electrons ($2$ in $s$, $6$ in $p$, and $10$ in $d$).</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section: Core Principles -->
    <section class="glass-card reveal-on-scroll">
      <h2 class="section-title"><span>03.</span> The Trio of Governing Quantum Laws</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 25px;">To accurately assign electrons to orbitals, three fundamental principles of quantum mechanics must be followed strictly:</p>
      
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="glass-card" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          <h3 style="color: var(--cyan); margin-bottom: 12px;">1. Aufbau Principle</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
            Derived from the German word <em>Aufbauen</em> (to build up). It dictates that electrons must fill atomic orbitals of the <strong>lowest energy levels first</strong> before moving to higher ones. 
          </p>
          <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 10px; color: var(--cyan);">Order of energy: $1s < 2s < 2p < 3s$... </p>
        </article>

        <article class="glass-card" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          <h3 style="color: var(--cyan); margin-bottom: 12px;">2. Pauli Exclusion</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
            Formulated by Wolfgang Pauli. It states that no two electrons in an atom can share the exact same four quantum numbers. Pragmatically: <strong>an orbital can hold at most 2 electrons</strong>, and they must have <strong>opposite spins</strong> ($\uparrow\downarrow$).
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="glass-card" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          <h3 style="color: var(--purple); margin-bottom: 12px;">3. Hund's Rule</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
            For degenerate orbitals (orbitals with the same energy, like the three $p$ orbitals), electrons will <strong>occupy empty orbitals singly with parallel spins first</strong> before pairing up. This minimizes electron-electron repulsion.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section: SPDF Diagonal Rule / SVG Diagram -->
    <section class="glass-card reveal-on-scroll">
      <h2 class="section-title"><span>04.</span> The SPDF Diagonal Rule (Aufbau Diagram)</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        Sometimes, orbitals in a higher principal shell have lower energy than those in a lower shell (e.g., $4s$ is filled before $3d$ because $4s$ is at a lower energy state). The <strong>Diagonal Rule</strong> (also known as the Madelung or $(n+l)$ rule) is a handy geometric visualizer used to determine the exact order of orbital filling.
      </p>

