            <span class="toggle-icon">▼</span>
          </div>
          <div class="example-body">
            <p><strong>Configuration:</strong> $[Ar] 4s^2 3d^{10}$</p>
            <p style="margin: 10px 0; color: var(--text-muted);">Zinc fully saturates both the $4s$ and the $3d$ subshells, ending the first row of transition metals.</p>
            <div class="orbital-visualizer">
              <div class="subshell-container">
                <div class="subshell-title">4s</div>
                <div class="orbital-boxes"><div class="orbital-box filled">↑↓</div></div>
              </div>
              <div class="subshell-container">
                <div class="subshell-title">3d</div>
                <div class="orbital-boxes">
                  <div class="orbital-box filled">↑↓</div>
                  <div class="orbital-box filled">↑↓</div>
                  <div class="orbital-box filled">↑↓</div>
                  <div class="orbital-box filled">↑↓</div>
                  <div class="orbital-box filled">↑↓</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section: Notes & Pitfalls -->
    <section id="notesSection" class="glass-card reveal-on-scroll">
      <h2 class="section-title"><span>06.</span> Important Notes & Common Mistakes</h2>
      
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div>
          <h3 style="color: var(--cyan); margin-bottom: 12px;">🌟 Key Notes (Why Cr & Cu are Exceptions)</h3>
          <ul style="padding-left: 20px; color: var(--text-muted);">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
              <strong style="color: #fff;">Symmetrical Distribution:</strong> Completely half-filled ($d^5$) and fully filled ($d^{10}$) orbitals have highly symmetrical charge clouds, minimizing repulsions.
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
              <strong style="color: #fff;">Exchange Energy:</strong> Electrons in degenerate subshells can swap positions. The number of possible exchanges is highest in half-filled and fully filled configurations, releasing stabilizing "exchange energy".
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
              <strong style="color: #fff;">Ionization Order:</strong> When transition metals (like Fe) lose electrons to form positive ions, electrons are lost from the outer <strong>4s orbital first</strong>, then 3d (even though 3d was filled last!).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 style="color: var(--danger); margin-bottom: 12px;">⚠️ Avoid These Common Mistakes</h3>
          <ul style="padding-left: 20px; color: var(--text-muted);">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
              <strong style="color: #fff;">Skipping the Aufbau order:</strong> Do not fill $3d$ before $4s$ unless you are dealing with Chromium or Copper!
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
              <strong style="color: #fff;">Spin Pairing Prematurely:</strong> Don't pair electrons in a subshell unless each orbital has at least one electron. (Violation of Hund's Rule).
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
              <strong style="color: #fff;">Ignoring Quantum Capacities:</strong> Never write a subshell exceeding capacity (e.g., $p^7$ or $d^{11}$ are completely impossible).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section: Revision Sheet -->
    <section class="glass-card reveal-on-scroll">
      <h2 class="section-title"><span>07.</span> Quick Revision Sheet</h2>
      <div class="grid-3" style="font-size: 0.95rem;">
        <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px;">
          <h4 style="color: var(--cyan); margin-bottom: 5px;">Azimuthal (l) Key</h4>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted);">$s \rightarrow 0$ | $p \rightarrow 1$ | $d \rightarrow 2$ | $f \rightarrow 3$</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px;">
          <h4 style="color: var(--cyan); margin-bottom: 5px;">Electron Capacities</h4>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted);">$s$: 2 | $p$: 6 | $d$: 10 | $f$: 14</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px;">
          <h4 style="color: var(--purple); margin-bottom: 5px;">Madelung Rule Formula</h4>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted);">Fill orbitals by increasing value of $(n + l)$.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section: Interactive MCQ Quiz -->
    <section id="quiz" class="glass-card quiz-section reveal-on-scroll">
      <h2 class="section-title"><span>08.</span> The Ultimate SPDF Practice Quiz</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 30px;">Test your quantum configuration skills. Select one correct option per question. Your work won't be evaluated until you tap the check button!</p>

      <div id="quizContainer">
        <!-- Question 1 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="B">
          <div class="question-text">Q1. What is the correct order of filling orbitals according to the Aufbau Principle?</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="A"> A) 1s, 2s, 2p, 3s, 3p, 3d, 4s</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="B"> B) 1s, 2s, 2p, 3s, 3p, 4s, 3d</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="C"> C) 1s, 2s, 3s, 3p, 4s, 3d, 4p</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q1" value="D"> D) 1s, 2s, 2p, 3s, 4s, 3p, 3d</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Question 2 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="C">
          <div class="question-text">Q2. Which rule states that "no two electrons in an atom can have the same four quantum numbers"?</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="A"> A) Hund's Rule</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="B"> B) Aufbau Principle</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="C"> C) Pauli Exclusion Principle</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q2" value="D"> D) Heisenberg Principle</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Question 3 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="B">
          <div class="question-text">Q3. What is the correct ground-state electronic configuration of Chromium (Z = 24)?</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="A"> A) [Ar] 4s² 3d⁴</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="B"> B) [Ar] 4s¹ 3d⁵</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="C"> C) [Ar] 4s⁰ 3d⁶</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q3" value="D"> D) [Ar] 4s² 3d⁵</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Question 4 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="A">
          <div class="question-text">Q4. Why is the actual electronic configuration of Copper (Z = 29) [Ar] 4s¹ 3d¹⁰ instead of [Ar] 4s² 3d⁹?</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="A"> A) Completely filled d-subshells (d¹⁰) have extra stability due to symmetry and high exchange energy.</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="B"> B) The 4s orbital has a higher energy level than the 3d orbital in Copper.</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="C"> C) Copper is a lanthanide element.</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q4" value="D"> D) Pauli exclusion rules strictly forbid d⁹ configurations.</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Question 5 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="C">
          <div class="question-text">Q5. According to Hund's Rule, when electrons enter degenerate orbitals (like three p-orbitals):</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q5" value="A"> A) They pair up immediately to conserve shell volume.</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q5" value="B"> B) They singly occupy empty orbitals with opposite spins first.</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q5" value="C"> C) They singly occupy empty orbitals with parallel spins first.</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q5" value="D"> D) They avoid p-orbitals and cascade directly into d-orbitals.</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Question 6 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="C">
          <div class="question-text">Q6. What is the maximum number of electrons that can be accommodated in the "d" subshell?</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q6" value="A"> A) 2</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q6" value="B"> B) 6</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q6" value="C"> C) 10</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q6" value="D"> D) 14</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Question 7 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="B">
          <div class="question-text">Q7. For a given principal quantum number n = 3, what are the allowed values of the azimuthal quantum number (l)?</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q7" value="A"> A) 1, 2, 3</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q7" value="B"> B) 0, 1, 2</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q7" value="C"> C) -1, 0, +1</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q7" value="D"> D) 0, 1, 2, 3</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Question 8 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="B">
          <div class="question-text">Q8. What is the correct ground-state configuration of a Zinc ion (Zn²⁺, Z = 30)?</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q8" value="A"> A) [Ar] 4s² 3d⁸</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q8" value="B"> B) [Ar] 4s⁰ 3d¹⁰</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q8" value="C"> C) [Ar] 4s¹ 3d⁹</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q8" value="D"> D) [Ar] 4s² 3d¹⁰</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Question 9 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="A">
          <div class="question-text">Q9. Which of the following subshells does NOT exist in quantum mechanical systems?</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q9" value="A"> A) 2d</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q9" value="B"> B) 3p</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q9" value="C"> C) 4f</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q9" value="D"> D) 5s</label>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Question 10 -->
        <div class="quiz-question-card" data-correct="B">
          <div class="question-text">Q10. What rule is violated in a carbon atom diagram showing 1s² 2s² 2px² 2py⁰ 2pz⁰?</div>
          <div class="options-grid">
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q10" value="A"> A) Aufbau Principle</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q10" value="B"> B) Hund's Rule of Maximum Multiplicity</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q10" value="C"> C) Pauli Exclusion Principle</label>
            <label class="option-label"><input type="radio" name="q10" value="D"> D) Heisenberg Principle</label>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Action Area -->
      <div style="margin-top: 30px; text-align: center;">
        <button id="checkQuizBtn" class="btn btn-purple" onclick="evaluateQuiz()">🏆 Evaluate & Check Solutions</button>
      </div>

      <!-- Result Scorecard -->
      <div id="scorecard" class="scorecard">
        <div class="score-circle" id="scoreCircle">0/10</div>
        <h3 id="resultHeading">Keep Practicing!</h3>
        <p id="resultMessage">You can always review the diagonal rules above and try again!</p>
        <div class="stats-row">
          <div class="stat-box">
            <div class="stat-num correct" id="correctCount">0</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted);">Correct</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-box">
            <div class="stat-num wrong" id="wrongCount">0</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted);">Incorrect</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-box">
            <div class="stat-num" id="percentageScore" style="color: var(--cyan);">0%</div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted);">Percentage</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <button class="btn" onclick="resetQuiz()">🔄 Restart Quiz</button>
      </div>

    </section>

  </main>

  <!-- Footer SEO Landmark -->
  <footer style="text-align: center; padding: 40px 0; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
    <p>&copy; 2026 QuantumSPDF Configuration & Aufbau Rule Masterclass. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>

  <!-- Floating Toast Notification -->
  <div id="toast">📋 Notes copied to clipboard!</div>

  <!-- Back to Top Button -->
  <button id="backToTop" class="back-to-top" onclick="scrollToTop()">▲</button>

  <script>
    // Scroll Progress logic
    window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
      const scrollProgress = document.getElementById('scrollProgress');
      const winScroll = document.documentElement.scrollTop || document.body.scrollTop;
      const height = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - document.documentElement.clientHeight;
      const scrolled = (winScroll / height) * 100;
      scrollProgress.style.width = scrolled + '%';

      // Back to Top trigger
      const btt = document.getElementById('backToTop');
      if (winScroll > 300) {
        btt.classList.add('show');
      } else {
        btt.classList.remove('show');
      }
    });

    function scrollToTop() {
      window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
    }

    // Scroll reveal mechanism
    const revealElements = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal-on-scroll');
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach(entry => {
        if(entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add('visible');
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.05 });

    revealElements.forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
    // Solved Examples Toggles
    function toggleExample(cardElement) {
      cardElement.classList.toggle('expanded');
    }
    // Copy Notes Action
    function copyConfigNotes() {
      const notes = `--- QUANTUM SPDF ELECTRONIC CONFIGURATION KEY SCHEME ---
Rules Summary:
1. Aufbau Principle: Electrons fill lowest energy orbitals first. 
Energy Order: 1s -> 2s -> 2p -> 3s -> 3p -> 4s -> 3d -> 4p -> 5s -> 4d...
2. Pauli Exclusion Principle: Max 2 electrons per orbital with opposite spins.
3. Hund's Rule: Occupy degenerate orbitals singly first with parallel spins.

Important Subshell capacities:
- s (l=0) holds max 2 electrons (1 orbital)
- p (l=1) holds max 6 electrons (3 orbitals)
- d (l=2) holds max 10 electrons (5 orbitals)
- f (l=3) holds max 14 electrons (7 orbitals)

Exceptional Cases:
- Chromium (Z=24): [Ar] 4s¹ 3d⁵ (half-filled d-orbital stability)
- Copper (Z=29): [Ar] 4s¹ 3d¹⁰ (fully-filled d-orbital stability)
------------------------------------------------------`;
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(notes).then(() => {
        showToast('📋 Core configuration notes copied!');
      }).catch(err => {
        showToast('❌ Copy failed. Check permissions.');
      });
    }
    function showToast(text) {
      const toast = document.getElementById('toast');
      toast.innerText = text;
      toast.classList.add('show');
      setTimeout(() => {
        toast.classList.remove('show');
      }, 3000);
    }
    function printPage() {
      window.print();
    }
    // Interactive MCQ Quiz Core Engine
    function evaluateQuiz() {
      const questions = document.querySelectorAll('.quiz-question-card');
      let score = 0;
      let unansweredCount = 0;
      // Ensure that all questions have at least one selection
      questions.forEach((q, index) => {
        const selected = q.querySelector('input[type="radio"]:checked');
        if (!selected) {
          unansweredCount++;
        }
      });
      if (unansweredCount > 0) {
        alert(`You have left ${unansweredCount} question(s) unanswered! Please select options for all questions before evaluating.`);
        return;
      }
      // Perform evaluation
      questions.forEach((q, index) => {
        const correctAnswer = q.getAttribute('data-correct');
        const selectedOption = q.querySelector('input[type="radio"]:checked');
        const selectedValue = selectedOption ? selectedOption.value : null;
        const labels = q.querySelectorAll('.option-label');
        labels.forEach(label => {
          const radioInput = label.querySelector('input');
          const value = radioInput.value;
          // Clear previous states
          label.classList.remove('correct-selected', 'incorrect-selected', 'correct-not-selected');
          // Disable inputs so user cannot edit answers after evaluation
          radioInput.disabled = true;
          if (value === correctAnswer) {
            if (selectedValue === correctAnswer) {
              label.classList.add('correct-selected'); // Green highlight
            } else {
              label.classList.add('correct-not-selected'); // Dotted green highlight for correct answers
            }
          } else if (value === selectedValue) {
            label.classList.add('incorrect-selected'); // Red highlight
          }
        });
        if (selectedValue === correctAnswer) {
          score++;
        }
      });
      // Scorecard generation logic
      const totalQuestions = questions.length;
      const incorrectScore = totalQuestions - score;
      const percentage = Math.round((score / totalQuestions) * 100);
      document.getElementById('scoreCircle').innerText = `${score}/${totalQuestions}`;
      document.getElementById('correctCount').innerText = score;
      document.getElementById('wrongCount').innerText = incorrectScore;
      document.getElementById('percentageScore').innerText = `${percentage}%`;
      // Custom performance messages
      let heading = "";
      let message = "";
      if (percentage === 100) {
        heading = "Mind-Blown! Absolute Perfection!";
        message = "You've completely mastered quantum electronic configurations, Master! Outstanding job.";
      } else if (percentage >= 70) {
        heading = "Brilliant Performance!";
        message = "Your quantum fundamentals are rock solid. A little more practice and you'll be completely unstoppable.";
      } else {
        heading = "Keep Pushing Forward!";
        message = "Quantum chemistry takes time to sink in. Review the diagonal rule and conquer it again!";
      }
      document.getElementById('resultHeading').innerText = heading;
      document.getElementById('resultMessage').innerText = message;
      document.getElementById('scorecard').style.display = 'block';
      document.getElementById('checkQuizBtn').style.display = 'none';
    }
    // Function to completely reset the quiz state
    function resetQuiz() {
      const questions = document.querySelectorAll('.quiz-question-card');
      questions.forEach(q => {
        const labels = q.querySelectorAll('.option-label');
        labels.forEach(label => {
          const radioInput = label.querySelector('input');
          radioInput.disabled = false;
          radioInput.checked = false;
          // Clean up all evaluation utility classes
          label.classList.remove('correct-selected', 'incorrect-selected', 'correct-not-selected');
        });
      });
      // Toggle UI visibility back to default state
      document.getElementById('scorecard').style.display = 'none';
      document.getElementById('checkQuizBtn').style.display = 'inline-block';
      // Smoothly scroll the Master back to the top of the quiz section
      document.getElementById('quiz').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>